+
+## DH options
+
+The three DH controls have their own **Distant Horizons** page, between
+**General** and **Far Players**, on both Sodium generations/loaders. General
+retains reception, LOD distance and download controls. Its reception toggle
+also greys out the DH controls before Apply. All pages share one save transaction.
+
+**Use DH** allows DH fallback when the server has no native LSS service. Native
+LSS always wins when advertised, including a disabled native offer. Changing this
+permission needs a reconnect. The DH protocol is automatic; there is no server-
+type selector. Official 15, official 16 and DH Support 15 are supported. Older
+servers may reconnect once automatically during discovery; this official-16
+manual server should connect directly. **Sync on load** and **Live updates** are checkboxes that apply immediately. Both default on and
+require the server to permit their services. The old Refresh slider and timer are
+removed; existing `lod.dh.refresh_seconds` and `lod.dh.profile` values are ignored.
+
+Sync on load checks terrain when it enters the LOD interest region or on rejoin,
+with DH's 20-minute load debounce. Standing still never causes periodic checks.
+Live updates subscribe to server-pushed edits for the negotiated radius, without
+requesting a full tile for each complete edit. `/lss dhstatus` reports whether the
